  "as_of": "2026-11-14",
  "source": "https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/pricing",
  "units": "USD per 1M tokens, Standard tier",
  "notes": [
    "Refresh this file from the source URL before trusting dollar figures. Scripts warn when as_of is older than 60 days.",
    "long_context applies when input exceeds long_context.threshold tokens. The pricing page does not say whether it covers the whole request; the scripts assume it does (conservative).",
    "Cache generation 'explicit' (GPT-5.6+ and GPT-6): cache reads cost read_multiplier x input, cache writes cost write_multipliers[ttl] x input, max 4 writes per request, prompt_cache_options replaces prompt_cache_retention.",
    "Cache generation 'implicit' (earlier models): no write charge, reads cost cached_input, retention via prompt_cache_retention ('in_memory' or '24h').",
    "Explicit-generation TTLs are minimum lifetimes. A 30m read refreshes coverage to at least 30 minutes after that read; a 30m read does not restart a 12h entry.",
    "Implicit 'in_memory' retention is 'typically 5 to 10 minutes of inactivity' per the caching guide; 300s is used here as the conservative end.",
    "Implicit-generation minimum prefix 'varies by request settings' per the caching guide; 1024 is an approximation.",
    "24h retention is per model. The caching guide lists gpt-5.5, gpt-5.5-pro, gpt-5.4, gpt-5.2, gpt-5.1 (and its codex/chat variants), gpt-5, gpt-5-codex and gpt-4.1. Other implicit models here are in_memory only.",
    "Batch and Flex are 50% of Standard. Fast mode (renamed from Priority on 2026-07-30) is roughly 2-2.5x Standard and varies by model; Ultrafast exists for gpt-6-astra and gpt-6.1-sol. Neither is modelled here.",
    "Verified against the pricing page and prompt-caching guide on 2026-11-14."
  ],
  "tiers": { "standard": 1.0, "batch": 0.5, "flex": 0.5 },
  "cache_generations": {
